ONBOARDING.md
Welcome to Royal Archer — A Guide for New Collaborators
Thank you for your interest in contributing to Royal Archer Editorial Studio.
This guide will help you get oriented, understand the project structure, and begin contributing with confidence.

1. What Royal Archer Is
Royal Archer is a creative and editorial platform offering:

editorial and publishing services

creative writing and storytelling

educational courses and articles

digital tools for writers and readers

community collaboration

future co‑ownership opportunities

This repository contains the technical and creative foundation of the platform.

2. Getting Started
Step 1 — Explore the Repository
Familiarize yourself with:

README.md — project overview

CONTRIBUTING.md — how to contribute

COLLABORATION‑TERMS.md — collaboration rules

CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md — community expectations

Step 2 — Set Up Your Environment
Depending on the project stage, setup instructions may include:

installing dependencies

running local development tools

reviewing documentation

(If needed, I can generate a setup section once your repo structure is finalized.)

3. Understanding the Project Structure
Typical folders may include:

/src — source code

/content — editorial or educational materials

/design — UI/UX assets

/docs — documentation

/community — collaboration resources

As the project grows, this structure can evolve.

4. How to Contribute
You can contribute through:

pull requests

issues

discussions

documentation updates

design proposals

editorial improvements

See CONTRIBUTING.md for full details.

5. Communication
Use GitHub Issues for:

questions

proposals

bugs

ideas

Clear communication helps the project grow smoothly.

6. Path to Deeper Collaboration
If you want to become more involved:

contribute consistently

participate in discussions

align with the project’s mission

express interest in long‑term collaboration

Future co‑ownership is possible through a separate written agreement.

7. Thank You
Your creativity, skill, and time are deeply appreciated.
Welcome to Royal Archer — we’re glad you’re here.
